.TH ARCHAIC-CLI 1 "September 2026" "Archaic 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
archaic-cli \- command-line interface for the Archaic autocomplete daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B archaic-cli
.RI [ --sock PATH ]
.RI COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B archaic-cli
is the command-line interface for interacting with the Archaic autocomplete daemon.
It provides commands to control the daemon, query completions, and manage state.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan \fIpath\fR
Trigger a filesystem scan starting at the specified path.
.TP
.B query \ficwd\fR \fIinput\fR
Validate a path query. Returns whether the path exists and its type.
.TP
.B complete \fIprefix\fR [\fIlimit\fR] [\fIcwd\fR] [\fIdirs_only\fR]
Get completions for the given prefix. Optional limit (default: 10), cwd for
proximity boosting, dirs_only (1 = directories only).
.TP
.B suggest \fIprefix\fR [\fIcwd\fR]
Get the best suggestion for the given prefix.
.TP
.B fuzzy \fIquery\fR [\fIlimit\fR]
Get fuzzy completions matching the query pattern.
.TP
.B select \fIpath\fR
Record that the user selected a path (feeds frequency/recency scoring).
.TP
.B recent [\fIn\fR]
Get the n most recently accessed files (default: 10).
.TP
.B ping
Check if the daemon is running and responsive.
.TP
.B metrics
Display daemon performance metrics and statistics.
.TP
.B stats
Same as metrics, plus cache hit-rate and index totals.
.TP
.B health
Detailed daemon health: pid, uptime, watcher, cache, memory, scan roots.
.TP
.B scan-status
Check the current scan progress and status.
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnose setup: config source, socket, scan paths, state file, ping, cache,
watcher, index totals. Start here when completions are empty.
.TP
.B explain \fIprefix\fR [\fIcwd\fR]
Explain why a prefix does or does not complete: roots, ignore rules,
on-disk state, daemon scanning flag, live result count.
.TP
.B watch \fIpath\fR
Add a tree to ~/.config/archaic/roots and trigger a scan.
.TP
.B unwatch \fIpath\fR
Remove a tree from ~/.config/archaic/roots.
.TP
.B roots
List configured scan roots (config file plus roots file).
.TP
.B save \fIpath\fR
Save daemon state to the specified file path.
.TP
.B clear-cache
Flush the query cache without restarting (uses IPC_MSG_CLEAR_CACHE).
.TP
.B reindex [\fIpath\fR]
Rescan a path, or all configured roots when omitted. Never defaults to /.
.TP
.B reload
Ask the daemon to reload configuration (sets reload flag; SIGHUP applies it).
.TP
.B reset-stats
Zero metrics counters and flush the query cache.
.TP
.B shutdown
Stop the daemon gracefully.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --sock \fIPATH\fR
Use PATH instead of the configured socket.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ARCHAIC_CONFIG
Path to configuration file (default: ~/.config/archaic/config.toml).
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Socket defaults to $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/archaic.sock, else /tmp/archaic-$UID.sock
(where UID is the numeric user id).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/archaic/config.toml
User configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/archaic/config.toml
System-wide configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/archaic/roots
Extra scan roots, one per line (managed by watch/unwatch).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/archaic.sock
Default daemon socket path (else /tmp/archaic-$UID.sock).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Start a scan:
.RS
.nf
$ archaic-cli scan ~/projects
.fi
.RE
.PP
Get completions:
.RS
.nf
$ archaic-cli complete ~/pro 10
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check daemon status:
.RS
.nf
$ archaic-cli ping
$ archaic-cli doctor
$ archaic-cli explain ~/pro
.fi
.RE
.PP
Manage roots and cache:
.RS
.nf
$ archaic-cli watch ~/src
$ archaic-cli roots
$ archaic-cli reindex
$ archaic-cli clear-cache
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR archaic (1),
.BR archaic-helper (1),
.BR archaic.conf (5)
